{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And He said: <b>You shall not make for yourself a graven image, nor any likeness that is in the heavens, etc.</b> Even though there are several kinds of idolatry that have no likeness either in the heavens or on earth, nevertheless He specified precisely these, because even if they were worshipping things of which the world has no need, the Holy One, blessed be He, would destroy them. But now that they also worship things of which the world does have need — such as the sun and the moon and their like — would He destroy His world on account of the fools who corrupted themselves? And if He would destroy those things of which the world has no need, how much the more so is it brazenness to worship things of which the world does have need, for one would say: since those were destroyed and these endured, surely there is substance to them. Therefore He specified precisely those that are in the heavens and on earth, which cannot be destroyed; and if they do not worship these, there is no need to worry about the rest of idolatry, for it is easy to destroy them like chaff that the wind drives away."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:34.602003679Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}